# TypeScript & React Native Style

## Naming
- Use meaningful names; avoid 1–2 letter variables.
- Functions are verbs; variables are nouns.

## Components
- Use `ThemedText`/`ThemedView` for UI text/containers.
- Reuse `AppInput` and `AppButton` for forms.
- Keep components small and focused; prefer composition.

## Control Flow
- Use early returns; avoid deep nesting (>2–3 levels).
- Handle error/edge cases first; no empty `catch` blocks.

## Formatting
- Match existing style: semicolons, multi-line for readability, wrap long lines.
- Do not reformat unrelated code in edits.

## Comments
- Explain "why", not "how"; avoid trivial comments.
- No inline narration comments inside code.

## Theming & Tokens
- Pull colors/spacings/fonts from [constants/Colors.ts](mdc:constants/Colors.ts) and [constants/GlobalStyles.ts](mdc:constants/GlobalStyles.ts).
- Respect dark/light via `Themed*` components.

## Forms
- Use `react-hook-form` with `yup` via `yupResolver`.
- Map errors to `AppInput`'s `errorMessage`.

## Accessibility
- Touch targets ≥ 44x44.
- Provide labels for interactive icons.
